      "extract": "arXiv:math/0611941v3 [math.RT] 19 Mar 2007 HECKE ALGEBRAS OF FINITE TYPE ARE CELLULAR MEINOLF GECK Abstract. Let H be the one-parameter Hecke algebra associated to a ﬁnite Weyl group W, deﬁned over a ground ring in which “bad” primes for W are invertible. Using deep properties of the Kazhdan–Lusztig basis of H and Lusztig’s a-function, we show that H has a natural cellular structure in the sense of Graham and",
