      "extract": "[]{#sec:intro label=\"sec:intro\"} The concept of \"cellular algebras\" was introduced by Graham and Lehrer [@GrLe]. It provides a systematic framework for studying the representation theory of non-semisimple algebras which are deformations of semisimple ones. The original definition was modeled on properties of the Kazhdan--Lusztig basis [@KaLu] in Hecke algebras of type $A_n$. There is now a significant literature on",
